From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carlos Chulo <cchulo.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 06:30:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] HID: asus-ally: add effect, speed, direction and enabled
 attributes to the ring LED

The joystick ring LED only exposes the led-class-multicolor attributes
plus sleep_animation, so the MCU's built-in Aura effects (breathe,
strobe, colour cycle, rainbow) can't be reached from Linux. The rings
are also the only Steam-visible RGB device here (now registered as
go_s:rgb:joystick_rings), and tools written for that node expect the
hid-lenovo-go-s attribute set: effect, effect_index, speed,
speed_range, enabled, enabled_index, mode, mode_index.

Add these attributes to the existing LED attribute group (the one that
holds sleep_animation):

  effect / effect_index        monocolor breathe chroma rainbow strobe
                               ("static" accepted as an alias)
  speed / speed_range          0-100, mapped to the MCU's three speeds
  direction / direction_index  forward reverse
  enabled / enabled_index      false true
  mode / mode_index            custom (go_s ABI compatibility only)

All of them are wired to the HID report helpers the driver already has.

- monocolor keeps the existing per-zone software path
  (xpad_cmd_set_leds on report 0x5a/0xd1) and the fixed hardware
  level from ally_rgb_set_bright_base_max(). Behaviour is unchanged
  unless an effect is selected.
- Animated effects use the Aura effect report on 0x5a:
    0x5a 0xb3 <zone=0> <effect> <r> <g> <b> <speed> <direction>
  followed by EC_MODE_LED_SET (0x5a 0xb5) and then EC_MODE_LED_APPLY
  (0x5a 0xb4). Effect numbers are the Aura wire values (0 static,
  1 breathe, 2 colour cycle, 3 rainbow, 10 strobe). Speeds are 0xe1,
  0xeb and 0xf5 (slow, normal, fast). The set-before-apply
  order comes from kndclark's testing: with apply first the Ally X shows
  a red pulse of the previous effect.
- Animated effects are dimmed with the MCU's 0-3 hardware level
  (report 0x5d 0xba 0xc5 0xc4 <level>), mapped from the LED brightness.
  The level is sent only when it changes, because the MCU may store it
  in flash.
- Effect, speed, direction and enabled live in the driver's static
  ally_rgb_data, next to the colour, so they survive suspend and
  re-probe. ally_pm_suspend() now leaves the MCU running the selected
  effect (or dark when disabled) instead of always forcing a static
  colour. Resume and probe resend the effect.

The ABI is documented in Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-hid-asus-ally.

Derived from:
- kndclark/ally_module, hid-asus.c (asus_usb_rgb_send_zone_effect(),
  effect table, speed/direction values, B3 -> B5 -> B4 ordering,
  0-3 brightness mapping), https://github.com/kndclark/ally_module
- ValveSoftware/SteamOS#2371 (effect/speed sysfs proposal for
  6.18-valve hid-asus-ally)
- z13ctl protocol notes, derived from g-helper (Aura mode bytes
  00/01/03/0a and speed bytes e1/eb/f5 on a related ASUS MCU),
  https://dahui.github.io/z13ctl/protocol
- drivers/hid/hid-lenovo-go-s.c and
  Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-hid-lenovo-go-s (attribute
  names and value spellings of the go_s:rgb:joystick_rings ABI)

Base: linux-integration 7.2.7-valve2 plus the previous patch in this
series.

TODO(hw): verify on an RC74XA that report 0x5a 0xb3 drives the rings
(the old suspend helper sends 0xb3 on 0x5d), that the five effects
match their names, the speed and direction encodings, and whether
the 0-3 level is persisted in MCU flash.
---
 .../ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-hid-asus-ally    | 127 ++++++
 drivers/hid/hid-asus-ally.c                   | 423 +++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 545 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-hid-asus-ally

diff --git a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-hid-asus-ally b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-hid-asus-ally
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8370bde
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-hid-asus-ally
@@ -0,0 +1,127 @@
+What:		/sys/class/leds/<led>/effect
+Date:		October 2026
+Contact:	linux-input@vger.kernel.org
+Description:	Aura effect shown on the joystick rings. Written as one of
+		the names listed in effect_index; "static" is accepted as an
+		alias for monocolor.
+
+		monocolor: one solid colour from multi_intensity, dimmed by
+		brightness. breathe and strobe: the multi_intensity colour,
+		animated by the MCU. chroma and rainbow: colour cycles
+		generated by the MCU; multi_intensity is ignored.
+
+		For animated effects brightness is mapped to the MCU's four
+		hardware levels (0, 1-85, 86-170, 171-255).
+
+		<led> is go_s:rgb:joystick_rings, or ally:rgb:joystick_rings
+		when hid-asus-ally is loaded with steam_led_name=0.
+
+		Applies to handhelds bound by hid-asus-ally (ROG Ally, Ally X
+		and devices sharing their N-KEY USB IDs).
+
+What:		/sys/class/leds/<led>/effect_index
+Date:		October 2026
+Contact:	linux-input@vger.kernel.org
+Description:	Space separated list of the values accepted by effect:
+		monocolor breathe chroma rainbow strobe.
+
+		<led> is go_s:rgb:joystick_rings, or ally:rgb:joystick_rings
+		when hid-asus-ally is loaded with steam_led_name=0.
+
+		Applies to handhelds bound by hid-asus-ally (ROG Ally, Ally X
+		and devices sharing their N-KEY USB IDs).
+
+What:		/sys/class/leds/<led>/speed
+Date:		October 2026
+Contact:	linux-input@vger.kernel.org
+Description:	Animation speed of breathe, strobe, chroma and rainbow,
+		0-100. The MCU has three speeds: 0-33 slow, 34-66 medium,
+		67-100 fast.
+
+		<led> is go_s:rgb:joystick_rings, or ally:rgb:joystick_rings
+		when hid-asus-ally is loaded with steam_led_name=0.
+
+		Applies to handhelds bound by hid-asus-ally (ROG Ally, Ally X
+		and devices sharing their N-KEY USB IDs).
+
+What:		/sys/class/leds/<led>/speed_range
+Date:		October 2026
+Contact:	linux-input@vger.kernel.org
+Description:	Range accepted by speed: 0-100.
+
+		<led> is go_s:rgb:joystick_rings, or ally:rgb:joystick_rings
+		when hid-asus-ally is loaded with steam_led_name=0.
+
+		Applies to handhelds bound by hid-asus-ally (ROG Ally, Ally X
+		and devices sharing their N-KEY USB IDs).
+
+What:		/sys/class/leds/<led>/direction
+Date:		October 2026
+Contact:	linux-input@vger.kernel.org
+Description:	Direction of the chroma and rainbow animations: forward or
+		reverse.
+
+		<led> is go_s:rgb:joystick_rings, or ally:rgb:joystick_rings
+		when hid-asus-ally is loaded with steam_led_name=0.
+
+		Applies to handhelds bound by hid-asus-ally (ROG Ally, Ally X
+		and devices sharing their N-KEY USB IDs).
+
+What:		/sys/class/leds/<led>/direction_index
+Date:		October 2026
+Contact:	linux-input@vger.kernel.org
+Description:	Values accepted by direction: forward reverse.
+
+		<led> is go_s:rgb:joystick_rings, or ally:rgb:joystick_rings
+		when hid-asus-ally is loaded with steam_led_name=0.
+
+		Applies to handhelds bound by hid-asus-ally (ROG Ally, Ally X
+		and devices sharing their N-KEY USB IDs).
+
+What:		/sys/class/leds/<led>/enabled
+Date:		October 2026
+Contact:	linux-input@vger.kernel.org
+Description:	Turns the joystick rings on (true) or off (false) without
+		losing colour, effect or brightness. Accepts the usual
+		kstrtobool spellings (1/0, y/n, true/false, on/off).
+
+		<led> is go_s:rgb:joystick_rings, or ally:rgb:joystick_rings
+		when hid-asus-ally is loaded with steam_led_name=0.
+
+		Applies to handhelds bound by hid-asus-ally (ROG Ally, Ally X
+		and devices sharing their N-KEY USB IDs).
+
+What:		/sys/class/leds/<led>/enabled_index
+Date:		October 2026
+Contact:	linux-input@vger.kernel.org
+Description:	Values accepted by enabled: false true.
+
+		<led> is go_s:rgb:joystick_rings, or ally:rgb:joystick_rings
+		when hid-asus-ally is loaded with steam_led_name=0.
+
+		Applies to handhelds bound by hid-asus-ally (ROG Ally, Ally X
+		and devices sharing their N-KEY USB IDs).
+
+What:		/sys/class/leds/<led>/mode
+Date:		October 2026
+Contact:	linux-input@vger.kernel.org
+Description:	Compatibility attribute matching the go_s:rgb:joystick_rings
+		ABI of hid-lenovo-go-s. Always "custom" (the host selects
+		colour and effect); writing anything else returns -EINVAL.
+
+		<led> is go_s:rgb:joystick_rings, or ally:rgb:joystick_rings
+		when hid-asus-ally is loaded with steam_led_name=0.
+
+		Applies to handhelds bound by hid-asus-ally (ROG Ally, Ally X
+		and devices sharing their N-KEY USB IDs).
+
+What:		/sys/class/leds/<led>/mode_index
+Date:		October 2026
+Contact:	linux-input@vger.kernel.org
+Description:	Values accepted by mode: custom.
+
+		<led> is go_s:rgb:joystick_rings, or ally:rgb:joystick_rings
+		when hid-asus-ally is loaded with steam_led_name=0.
+
+		Applies to handhelds bound by hid-asus-ally (ROG Ally, Ally X
+		and devices sharing their N-KEY USB IDs).
diff --git a/drivers/hid/hid-asus-ally.c b/drivers/hid/hid-asus-ally.c
index c649347..8c1cd00 100644
--- a/drivers/hid/hid-asus-ally.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/hid-asus-ally.c
@@ -54,6 +54,44 @@
  */
 #define ALLY_RGB_LED_NAME_STEAM "go_s:rgb:joystick_rings"
 
+/* Aura effect report (0x5a 0xb3), latched by EC_MODE_LED_SET then EC_MODE_LED_APPLY */
+#define ALLY_RGB_CMD_CONFIG 0xb3
+#define ALLY_RGB_ZONE_ALL 0x00
+
+/* Aura effect speed register values (slow, normal, fast) */
+#define ALLY_RGB_SPEED_SLOW 0xe1
+#define ALLY_RGB_SPEED_MED 0xeb
+#define ALLY_RGB_SPEED_FAST 0xf5
+
+/* Hardware brightness levels of report 0x5d 0xba 0xc5 0xc4 <level> */
+#define ALLY_RGB_HW_LEVEL_MAX 3
+#define ALLY_RGB_HW_LEVEL_UNKNOWN 0xff
+
+/* Aura effect numbers on the wire, as used by g-helper and kndclark/ally_module */
+enum ally_rgb_effect {
+	ALLY_RGB_EFFECT_MONOCOLOR = 0x00,
+	ALLY_RGB_EFFECT_BREATHE = 0x01,
+	ALLY_RGB_EFFECT_CHROMA = 0x02,
+	ALLY_RGB_EFFECT_RAINBOW = 0x03,
+	ALLY_RGB_EFFECT_STROBE = 0x0a,
+};
+
+enum ally_rgb_direction {
+	ALLY_RGB_DIRECTION_REVERSE = 0x00,
+	ALLY_RGB_DIRECTION_FORWARD = 0x01,
+};
+
+static const struct {
+	u8 effect;
+	const char *name;
+} ally_rgb_effects[] = {
+	{ ALLY_RGB_EFFECT_MONOCOLOR, "monocolor" },
+	{ ALLY_RGB_EFFECT_BREATHE, "breathe" },
+	{ ALLY_RGB_EFFECT_CHROMA, "chroma" },
+	{ ALLY_RGB_EFFECT_RAINBOW, "rainbow" },
+	{ ALLY_RGB_EFFECT_STROBE, "strobe" },
+};
+
 static bool steam_led_name = true;
 module_param(steam_led_name, bool, 0444);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(steam_led_name,
@@ -405,6 +443,10 @@ struct ally_rgb_dev {
 	bool removed;
 	bool attr_group_added;
 	bool update_rgb;
+	/* effect, speed, direction or enabled changed */
+	bool update_aura;
+	/* last level sent to the MCU, ALLY_RGB_HW_LEVEL_UNKNOWN after (re)init */
+	u8 hw_level;
 	uint8_t red[ALLY_RGB_NUM_ZONES];
 	uint8_t green[ALLY_RGB_NUM_ZONES];
 	uint8_t blue[ALLY_RGB_NUM_ZONES];
@@ -418,6 +460,12 @@ struct ally_rgb_data {
 	uint8_t green[ALLY_RGB_NUM_ZONES];
 	uint8_t blue[ALLY_RGB_NUM_ZONES];
 	bool initialized;
+	/* Aura state, kept here so it survives suspend and re-probe */
+	bool aura_valid;
+	u8 effect;
+	u8 speed; /* 0-100 */
+	u8 direction;
+	bool enabled;
 };
 
 static struct ally_drvdata {
@@ -1759,6 +1807,82 @@ static int ally_rgb_set_bright_base_max(struct hid_device *hdev)
 	return asus_dev_set_report(hdev, buf, sizeof(buf));
 }
 
+/*
+ * Animated effects run on the MCU and are dimmed by this 0-3 hardware level,
+ * not by the software colour scaling done in ally_rgb_set().
+ */
+static int ally_rgb_set_bright_level(struct hid_device *hdev, u8 level)
+{
+	u8 buf[] = { FEATURE_KBD_LED_REPORT_ID1, 0xba, 0xc5, 0xc4, level };
+
+	return asus_dev_set_report(hdev, buf, sizeof(buf));
+}
+
+static u8 ally_rgb_bright_to_level(unsigned int brightness)
+{
+	if (!brightness)
+		return 0;
+	if (brightness <= 85)
+		return 1;
+	if (brightness <= 170)
+		return 2;
+	return ALLY_RGB_HW_LEVEL_MAX;
+}
+
+static u8 ally_rgb_speed_to_hw(u8 speed)
+{
+	if (speed <= 33)
+		return ALLY_RGB_SPEED_SLOW;
+	if (speed <= 66)
+		return ALLY_RGB_SPEED_MED;
+	return ALLY_RGB_SPEED_FAST;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Program a hardware Aura effect for the whole ring: effect report (0xb3),
+ * then set (0xb5), then apply (0xb4). Sending apply before set makes the
+ * MCU briefly show its previous/default effect (a red pulse on Ally X).
+ */
+static int ally_rgb_send_aura(struct hid_device *hdev, u8 effect, u8 red, u8 green,
+			      u8 blue, u8 speed, u8 direction)
+{
+	u8 buf[FEATURE_ROG_ALLY_REPORT_SIZE] = { [0] = FEATURE_ROG_ALLY_REPORT_ID,
+						 [1] = ALLY_RGB_CMD_CONFIG,
+						 [2] = ALLY_RGB_ZONE_ALL };
+	int ret;
+
+	buf[3] = effect;
+	buf[4] = red;
+	buf[5] = green;
+	buf[6] = blue;
+	buf[7] = ally_rgb_speed_to_hw(speed);
+	buf[8] = direction;
+
+	ret = asus_dev_set_report(hdev, buf, sizeof(buf));
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return ret;
+
+	ret = asus_dev_set_report(hdev, EC_MODE_LED_SET, sizeof(EC_MODE_LED_SET));
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return ret;
+
+	return asus_dev_set_report(hdev, EC_MODE_LED_APPLY, sizeof(EC_MODE_LED_APPLY));
+}
+
+static void ally_rgb_aura_defaults(void)
+{
+	struct ally_rgb_data *cfg = &drvdata.led_rgb_data;
+
+	if (cfg->aura_valid)
+		return;
+
+	cfg->effect = ALLY_RGB_EFFECT_MONOCOLOR;
+	cfg->speed = 50;
+	cfg->direction = ALLY_RGB_DIRECTION_FORWARD;
+	cfg->enabled = true;
+	cfg->aura_valid = true;
+}
+
 /*
  * Persistent mask of power states in which the MCU animates the joystick
  * rings (factory default: all). With the sleep bit set the MCU breathes the
@@ -1825,9 +1949,231 @@ static ssize_t sleep_animation_index_show(struct device *dev,
 }
 DEVICE_ATTR_RO(sleep_animation_index);
 
+static struct ally_rgb_dev *ally_rgb_from_dev(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct led_classdev *cdev = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	return container_of(lcdev_to_mccdev(cdev), struct ally_rgb_dev, led_rgb_dev);
+}
+
+static void ally_rgb_queue_aura(struct ally_rgb_dev *led)
+{
+	unsigned long flags;
+
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&led->lock, flags);
+	led->update_aura = true;
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&led->lock, flags);
+
+	ally_rgb_schedule_work(led);
+}
+
+static ssize_t ally_rgb_effect_show(struct device *dev, struct device_attribute *attr,
+				    char *buf)
+{
+	u8 effect = drvdata.led_rgb_data.effect;
+
+	for (int i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(ally_rgb_effects); i++) {
+		if (ally_rgb_effects[i].effect == effect)
+			return sysfs_emit(buf, "%s\n", ally_rgb_effects[i].name);
+	}
+
+	return -EINVAL;
+}
+
+static ssize_t ally_rgb_effect_store(struct device *dev, struct device_attribute *attr,
+				     const char *buf, size_t count)
+{
+	struct ally_rgb_dev *led = ally_rgb_from_dev(dev);
+	unsigned long flags;
+	int i;
+
+	/* "static" is accepted as an alias, it is the name asusctl and Windows use */
+	if (sysfs_streq(buf, "static")) {
+		i = 0;
+	} else {
+		for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(ally_rgb_effects); i++) {
+			if (sysfs_streq(buf, ally_rgb_effects[i].name))
+				break;
+		}
+		if (i == ARRAY_SIZE(ally_rgb_effects))
+			return -EINVAL;
+	}
+
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&led->lock, flags);
+	drvdata.led_rgb_data.effect = ally_rgb_effects[i].effect;
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&led->lock, flags);
+
+	ally_rgb_queue_aura(led);
+
+	return count;
+}
+ALLY_DEVICE_ATTR_RW(ally_rgb_effect, effect);
+
+static ssize_t ally_rgb_effect_index_show(struct device *dev, struct device_attribute *attr,
+					  char *buf)
+{
+	int len = 0;
+
+	for (int i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(ally_rgb_effects); i++)
+		len += sysfs_emit_at(buf, len, "%s%s", i ? " " : "", ally_rgb_effects[i].name);
+	len += sysfs_emit_at(buf, len, "\n");
+
+	return len;
+}
+ALLY_DEVICE_ATTR_RO(ally_rgb_effect_index, effect_index);
+
+static ssize_t ally_rgb_speed_show(struct device *dev, struct device_attribute *attr,
+				   char *buf)
+{
+	return sysfs_emit(buf, "%u\n", drvdata.led_rgb_data.speed);
+}
+
+static ssize_t ally_rgb_speed_store(struct device *dev, struct device_attribute *attr,
+				    const char *buf, size_t count)
+{
+	struct ally_rgb_dev *led = ally_rgb_from_dev(dev);
+	unsigned long flags;
+	u8 val;
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = kstrtou8(buf, 0, &val);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	if (val > 100)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&led->lock, flags);
+	drvdata.led_rgb_data.speed = val;
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&led->lock, flags);
+
+	ally_rgb_queue_aura(led);
+
+	return count;
+}
+ALLY_DEVICE_ATTR_RW(ally_rgb_speed, speed);
+
+static ssize_t ally_rgb_speed_range_show(struct device *dev, struct device_attribute *attr,
+					 char *buf)
+{
+	return sysfs_emit(buf, "0-100\n");
+}
+ALLY_DEVICE_ATTR_RO(ally_rgb_speed_range, speed_range);
+
+static ssize_t ally_rgb_direction_show(struct device *dev, struct device_attribute *attr,
+				       char *buf)
+{
+	return sysfs_emit(buf, "%s\n",
+			  drvdata.led_rgb_data.direction == ALLY_RGB_DIRECTION_REVERSE ?
+			  "reverse" : "forward");
+}
+
+static ssize_t ally_rgb_direction_store(struct device *dev, struct device_attribute *attr,
+					const char *buf, size_t count)
+{
+	struct ally_rgb_dev *led = ally_rgb_from_dev(dev);
+	unsigned long flags;
+	u8 dir;
+
+	if (sysfs_streq(buf, "forward"))
+		dir = ALLY_RGB_DIRECTION_FORWARD;
+	else if (sysfs_streq(buf, "reverse"))
+		dir = ALLY_RGB_DIRECTION_REVERSE;
+	else
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&led->lock, flags);
+	drvdata.led_rgb_data.direction = dir;
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&led->lock, flags);
+
+	ally_rgb_queue_aura(led);
+
+	return count;
+}
+ALLY_DEVICE_ATTR_RW(ally_rgb_direction, direction);
+
+static ssize_t ally_rgb_direction_index_show(struct device *dev,
+					     struct device_attribute *attr, char *buf)
+{
+	return sysfs_emit(buf, "forward reverse\n");
+}
+ALLY_DEVICE_ATTR_RO(ally_rgb_direction_index, direction_index);
+
+static ssize_t ally_rgb_enabled_show(struct device *dev, struct device_attribute *attr,
+				     char *buf)
+{
+	return sysfs_emit(buf, "%s\n", drvdata.led_rgb_data.enabled ? "true" : "false");
+}
+
+static ssize_t ally_rgb_enabled_store(struct device *dev, struct device_attribute *attr,
+				      const char *buf, size_t count)
+{
+	struct ally_rgb_dev *led = ally_rgb_from_dev(dev);
+	unsigned long flags;
+	bool val;
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = kstrtobool(buf, &val);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&led->lock, flags);
+	drvdata.led_rgb_data.enabled = val;
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&led->lock, flags);
+
+	ally_rgb_queue_aura(led);
+
+	return count;
+}
+ALLY_DEVICE_ATTR_RW(ally_rgb_enabled, enabled);
+
+static ssize_t ally_rgb_enabled_index_show(struct device *dev, struct device_attribute *attr,
+					   char *buf)
+{
+	return sysfs_emit(buf, "false true\n");
+}
+ALLY_DEVICE_ATTR_RO(ally_rgb_enabled_index, enabled_index);
+
+/*
+ * Compatibility with the go_s:rgb:joystick_rings ABI (hid-lenovo-go-s),
+ * whose "custom" mode is the only one that lets the host pick colour and
+ * effect. The Ally MCU has no equivalent of Lenovo's "dynamic" mode.
+ */
+static ssize_t ally_rgb_mode_show(struct device *dev, struct device_attribute *attr,
+				  char *buf)
+{
+	return sysfs_emit(buf, "custom\n");
+}
+
+static ssize_t ally_rgb_mode_store(struct device *dev, struct device_attribute *attr,
+				   const char *buf, size_t count)
+{
+	if (!sysfs_streq(buf, "custom"))
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	return count;
+}
+ALLY_DEVICE_ATTR_RW(ally_rgb_mode, mode);
+
+static ssize_t ally_rgb_mode_index_show(struct device *dev, struct device_attribute *attr,
+					char *buf)
+{
+	return sysfs_emit(buf, "custom\n");
+}
+ALLY_DEVICE_ATTR_RO(ally_rgb_mode_index, mode_index);
+
 static struct attribute *ally_rgb_attrs[] = {
 	&dev_attr_sleep_animation.attr,
 	&dev_attr_sleep_animation_index.attr,
+	&dev_attr_ally_rgb_effect.attr,
+	&dev_attr_ally_rgb_effect_index.attr,
+	&dev_attr_ally_rgb_speed.attr,
+	&dev_attr_ally_rgb_speed_range.attr,
+	&dev_attr_ally_rgb_direction.attr,
+	&dev_attr_ally_rgb_direction_index.attr,
